[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Business Requirements
UID: YAAP-BR
DATE: @GIT_COMMIT_DATETIME
PREFIX: BR-

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Introduction

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
This document defines the business requirements for Yet Another Audio Player (YAAP),
a time accurate desktop audio player.

It is to provide users with music library and playback experience.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Audio Playback

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Supported Audio Playback

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: BR-001
TITLE: Local Audio Playback
STATEMENT: >>>
Yaap shall provide the ability to play supported audio files stored locally on their
devices.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: BR-002
TITLE: Cloud Audio Playback
STATEMENT: >>>
Yaap shall provide the ability to play supported audio files stored on supported,
linked Cloud providers.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Audio Playback Functionality

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: BR-003
TITLE: High-Quality Audio Playback
STATEMENT: >>>
Yaap shall provide accurate audio playback appropriate for high-quality music
collections.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: BR-004
TITLE: Accurate Audio Position
STATEMENT: >>>
Yaap shall provide an accurate representation of the current or requested playback
position of an audio track.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Music Organisation

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: BR-005
TITLE: Music Library
STATEMENT: Yaap shall be able to maintain and access a library of audio files.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: BR-006
TITLE: Music Organisation
STATEMENT: >>>
Yaap shall be able to organise audio tracks into playlists and collections.
<<<

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
A playlist is a list of songs. 
A collection is a list of playlists or collections.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]
